# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Everything in public/ is copied verbatim into out/, so this file lands at the
# root of the deployment where Pages looks for it. It costs no build step and
# no server: Pages reads it at the edge.
#
# /work was the single page that carried the whole portfolio before it was
# split into six collections. It has been linked from Nat's Instagram bio and
# from anything that indexed the site in the meantime, so it redirects rather
# than 404s. 301, because the move is permanent and the old URL should stop
# being served from search results.
#
# `trailingSlash: true` in next.config.ts means the canonical form of every
# route ends in a slash, hence both spellings below.
/work    /styles/  301
/work/   /styles/  301
